1
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,126
[THUNDER CRASHING]

2
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:37,623
[WIND WHISTLING]

3
00:00:56,608 --> 00:00:57,747
[♪♪♪]

4
00:01:15,972 --> 00:01:17,594
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

5
00:01:42,412 --> 00:01:44,863
[♪♪♪]

6
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,451
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

7
00:02:25,662 --> 00:02:26,870
[GRUNTING]

8
00:02:31,289 --> 00:02:33,291
Is it bad tonight?

9
00:02:33,325 --> 00:02:36,742
Oh, bad?
That's one way to describe it.

10
00:02:36,777 --> 00:02:40,850
Uh, "insane" seems
a little more appropriate.

11
00:02:40,884 --> 00:02:43,749
Feels like he's breathing
down my neck, man.

12
00:02:43,784 --> 00:02:48,202
It's my professional opinion
we should get the hell out of
here.

13
00:02:48,237 --> 00:02:51,964
Now!
Noted.

14
00:02:51,999 --> 00:02:54,691
Clean this place up
and locate our guests.

15
00:02:57,073 --> 00:03:01,008
Oh!

16
00:03:01,042 --> 00:03:02,492
Aah!

17
00:03:02,527 --> 00:03:04,667
I just need to take the edge
off.

18
00:03:04,701 --> 00:03:09,465
You know the routine.
I need you clearheaded.

19
00:03:09,499 --> 00:03:11,743
First things first.

20
00:03:14,849 --> 00:03:17,266
Now, where is he?

21
00:03:18,577 --> 00:03:22,616
Uh...Show me where he's hiding.

22
00:03:29,174 --> 00:03:30,520
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

23
00:03:32,626 --> 00:03:34,006
[SCREAMING]

24
00:03:38,114 --> 00:03:41,945
Son of a bitch! You said
he only killed nine people!
There's 40 victims here!

25
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:45,294
Nine when he was alive.
He's added a few since then.

26
00:03:45,328 --> 00:03:48,020
Now where is he, Dennis?

27
00:03:52,335 --> 00:03:54,095
[♪♪♪]

28
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:55,959
[THUNDER CRASHING]

29
00:03:57,754 --> 00:04:01,655
All teams go to alpha.
Bring in the cube!

30
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:07,902
How did this guy get
this name, The Breaker?
What, is he a truck driver?

31
00:04:07,937 --> 00:04:12,321
Simple folklore.
The local colour
exorcizing its demons.

32
00:04:12,355 --> 00:04:15,738
Or maybe it's because he
broke his victims into as
many pieces as possible.

33
00:04:15,772 --> 00:04:17,602
[SCREAMING]

34
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,675
I hate being rushed.

35
00:04:21,709 --> 00:04:23,849
DENNIS:
This wasn't like the others.

36
00:04:23,884 --> 00:04:26,749
Then I'll give you a bonus.You don't have that kind ofmoney.

37
00:04:26,783 --> 00:04:30,511
After tonight,
you'll be surprised.
Now get to work.

38
00:04:30,546 --> 00:04:31,961
[♪♪♪]

39
00:04:34,343 --> 00:04:35,758
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

40
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:39,348
Careful, Dennis.

41
00:04:39,382 --> 00:04:42,696
Don't get too curious.

42
00:04:43,973 --> 00:04:47,701
No! Son of a bitch!

43
00:04:47,735 --> 00:04:51,567
How can you possibly justify
what you're doing, Cyrus?
It's out and out slavery.

44
00:04:51,601 --> 00:04:55,398
I'll give you this, Damon.
You are persistent.
And what about you, Kalina?

45
00:04:55,433 --> 00:04:59,575
Still carrying around those
ridiculous quicksilver flares?

46
00:04:59,609 --> 00:05:01,818
You still have that
little magic book?

47
00:05:01,853 --> 00:05:05,374
These aren't animals
you're capturing.
They're human beings!

48
00:05:05,408 --> 00:05:07,203
Dead human beings.

49
00:05:07,237 --> 00:05:11,311
Maybe you should join
Greenpeace.
Throw blood on old women's furs.

50
00:05:11,345 --> 00:05:12,657
[CHUCKLING]

51
00:05:12,691 --> 00:05:15,038
[SPITS]
Who are you to play God?

52
00:05:16,902 --> 00:05:20,768
Playing's for children.DAMON: You'll never pull it off.

53
00:05:20,803 --> 00:05:24,393
Not without the right spells.
That and the 13th ghost.

54
00:05:24,427 --> 00:05:26,049
13th ghost?

55
00:05:26,084 --> 00:05:30,537
Get them out of my sight!
We've wasted too much time.

56
00:05:30,571 --> 00:05:32,711
Why did he say 13th?

57
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:34,886
Move the cube into position.

58
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,544
What's he talking about,
13 ghosts?

59
00:05:37,578 --> 00:05:41,513
You contracted me for 12 ghosts.
The Breaker's 12!

60
00:05:41,548 --> 00:05:43,101
I'm done after tonight, Cyrus.

61
00:05:43,135 --> 00:05:47,864
Yes, 12 and then one more.
I thought you were psychic.

62
00:05:47,899 --> 00:05:50,039
That's not how it works
and you know it.

63
00:05:50,073 --> 00:05:52,593
There's no time to argue.

64
00:05:52,628 --> 00:05:54,595
Release the bait.

65
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:57,840
What bait?
We never needed bait before!

66
00:05:57,874 --> 00:05:59,082
[ENGINE REVING]

67
00:06:01,257 --> 00:06:03,086
[♪♪♪]

68
00:06:09,783 --> 00:06:14,028
A truck full of blood?
You've gotta be shitting me.

69
00:06:17,031 --> 00:06:18,792
Oh, boy.

70
00:06:23,866 --> 00:06:25,626
Now...

71
00:06:25,661 --> 00:06:27,559
power up the cube.

72
00:06:34,601 --> 00:06:37,949
Start transmitting.

73
00:06:37,983 --> 00:06:39,606
[GHOSTLY VOICE CHANTING
IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE
ON RECORDER]

74
00:07:02,042 --> 00:07:03,457
[WHOOSHING]

75
00:07:06,909 --> 00:07:08,704
Come.

76
00:07:09,843 --> 00:07:11,361
Come.

77
00:07:11,396 --> 00:07:14,434
Come!

78
00:07:14,468 --> 00:07:16,608
[MEN SCREAMING]

79
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:22,200
MAN 1:
Oh, God! Help me!

80
00:07:22,234 --> 00:07:24,098
Help me!

81
00:07:27,516 --> 00:07:29,690
[PANTING]

82
00:07:29,725 --> 00:07:32,417
MAN 2:
Oh, shit!

83
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,970
[MAN 2 GRUNTING]

84
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:44,118
Oh!

85
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,915
[SCREAMING]

86
00:07:58,823 --> 00:08:01,515
MAN 3:
Where is it?
I can't see it!

87
00:08:01,550 --> 00:08:03,517
[MEN SCREAMING]

88
00:08:27,783 --> 00:08:30,233
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

89
00:08:30,268 --> 00:08:31,925
[SCREAMING]

90
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:38,448
Hey! Hey! Put him down!

91
00:08:38,483 --> 00:08:40,968
Hey! Hey!

92
00:08:44,558 --> 00:08:45,939
[GRUNTING]

93
00:08:51,979 --> 00:08:56,259
Hey, Cyrus. I hope you're happy.
You got your 12 now.

94
00:08:56,294 --> 00:08:59,159
KALINA:
Help me! He's dying!

95
00:08:59,193 --> 00:09:02,887
Hang on, Damon.
Somebody help!
Goddamn you, Cyrus!

96
00:09:02,921 --> 00:09:05,096
[GRUNTING]Somebody help me, please!

97
00:09:07,029 --> 00:09:09,790
Help me.
Do something!

98
00:09:14,036 --> 00:09:15,693
Oh.

99
00:09:17,798 --> 00:09:20,007
DENNIS:
Oh, Cyrus.

100
00:09:20,042 --> 00:09:21,630
Oh, God.

101
00:09:23,528 --> 00:09:25,357
Oh, Cyrus.

102
00:09:31,087 --> 00:09:32,882
BOBBY: Swing me.KATHY: Come on, Bobby.

103
00:09:32,917 --> 00:09:35,678
BOBBY:
Come on, Kathy. Faster!

104
00:09:35,713 --> 00:09:38,957
Let me get your arms.Come on. Try to drag me.

105
00:09:38,992 --> 00:09:42,305
You're the best little brother.
I love you.

106
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,686
Let's go.
Come on.

107
00:09:43,721 --> 00:09:45,792
I'm gonna get you!
I'm gonna get you!

108
00:09:45,826 --> 00:09:47,000
[BOTH LAUGHING]

109
00:09:47,034 --> 00:09:48,415
[CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]

110
00:09:48,449 --> 00:09:49,899
[♪♪♪]

111
00:09:49,934 --> 00:09:52,246
ARTHUR:
Look at them.
She's got him on the run now

112
00:09:52,281 --> 00:09:54,145
but before you know it,
he's gonna be picking her up

113
00:09:54,179 --> 00:09:56,526
and throwing her
over his shoulder.

114
00:09:56,561 --> 00:09:58,839
They're perfect.

115
00:09:58,874 --> 00:10:01,531
No, watch. Watch them.

116
00:10:01,566 --> 00:10:05,881
[GIGGLES]
They really love this place.

117
00:10:12,542 --> 00:10:14,096
I love you, you know?

118
00:10:14,130 --> 00:10:17,582
PEOPLE:
Surprise!

119
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:19,619
ARTHUR:
My heart! My heart!

120
00:10:19,653 --> 00:10:22,794
BOBBY: Happy birthday, Dad. KATHY: Happy birthday!

121
00:10:22,829 --> 00:10:26,384
JEAN: Happy birthday, Arthur. BOBBY: Here's my present.

122
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:31,009
KATHY: We love you. Make a wish. JEAN: Blow out the candles.

123
00:10:31,044 --> 00:10:32,942
KATHY:
What'd you wish for?

124
00:10:32,977 --> 00:10:35,600
JEAN: I love you. ARTHUR: I love you too.

125
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,602
[SMOKE ALARM BEEPING]

126
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:38,948
[FIRE ROARING]

127
00:10:40,812 --> 00:10:43,228
JEAN:
What's that?
Why's the smoke alarm on?

128
00:10:43,263 --> 00:10:45,092
ARTHUR:
It's the fire alarm.

129
00:10:45,127 --> 00:10:46,611
 I'll get the kids,
you call the fire department.

130
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,130
BOBBY:
Dad! Help, Mom!

131
00:10:48,164 --> 00:10:49,890
JEAN: Get the kids. BOBBY: Mom! Dad!

132
00:10:49,925 --> 00:10:51,581
JEAN:
Get the kids!

133
00:10:51,616 --> 00:10:54,688
BOBBY: Mom! Dad! Help me! KATHY: Dad, come on!

134
00:10:54,723 --> 00:10:58,519
ARTHUR: Where's your mom? KATHY: I don't know!

135
00:10:58,554 --> 00:11:00,004
 Bobby, we have to get out.

136
00:11:00,038 --> 00:11:01,212
JEAN:
Oh, my God!

137
00:11:01,246 --> 00:11:03,041
ARTHUR:
Jean! Jean!

138
00:11:03,076 --> 00:11:04,871
KATHY:
Mom's still in the house.

139
00:11:04,905 --> 00:11:06,700
 We can't leave her here. [SIRENS WAILING]

140
00:11:06,735 --> 00:11:09,358
KATHY:
Bobby, go outside.
Go wait outside, now.

141
00:11:09,392 --> 00:11:11,015
ARTHUR:
Jean!

142
00:11:11,049 --> 00:11:12,533
MAN:
You can't go back in there,
sir.

143
00:11:12,568 --> 00:11:13,983
[EKG BEEPING]

144
00:11:18,263 --> 00:11:19,886
[EKG FLATLINING]

145
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:23,061
DOCTOR:
I'm sorry, sir.
She didn't make it.

146
00:11:23,096 --> 00:11:26,582
ARTHUR:
I should have gone back in.

147
00:11:26,616 --> 00:11:29,896
[♪♪♪]

148
00:11:29,930 --> 00:11:35,729
MAN:
We're here to honour the memory
and life's work of Jean
Kriticos

149
00:11:35,764 --> 00:11:42,046
 a devoted mother and loving
wife,
who was too quickly taken from
life.

150
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:47,327
 Jean, you will be forever
missed,
but never forgotten.

151
00:11:47,361 --> 00:11:50,917
KATHY: I miss you, Mom. BOBBY: I miss you, Mom.

152
00:11:50,951 --> 00:11:55,128
KATHY:
Why did you have to leave us?

153
00:11:55,162 --> 00:11:58,372
 I can't do this without you. BOBBY: Don't go.

154
00:11:58,407 --> 00:12:01,893
KATHY:
Mom, I love you so much.

155
00:12:01,928 --> 00:12:05,552
 Please watch over us.

156
00:12:05,586 --> 00:12:08,797
 I'll love you always.

157
00:12:10,005 --> 00:12:11,834
[♪♪♪]

158
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,360
Dad, it's al--

159
00:12:20,394 --> 00:12:25,192
It's almost 8:30. Shake a leg
or you'll miss your first class.

160
00:12:25,227 --> 00:12:28,817
Today on Death in America:
Cancer rates are down

161
00:12:28,851 --> 00:12:30,784
but suicide is sky-high.

162
00:12:30,819 --> 00:12:33,407
We have a special
treat for you today.

163
00:12:33,442 --> 00:12:36,756
A body was found this
morning, "decolopolated."

164
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:39,931
Hey, hey. "Decapitated."

165
00:12:39,966 --> 00:12:42,451
Bobby, find a healthier hobby.

166
00:12:42,485 --> 00:12:44,971
Leave me alone, you guys.
I'm recording!

167
00:12:45,005 --> 00:12:50,493
Good morning, everybody.
Something smells interesting.

168
00:12:50,528 --> 00:12:54,014
They found a guy without
a head behind Dunkin' Donuts.

169
00:12:54,049 --> 00:12:56,810
Oh, I love Dunkin' Donuts.

170
00:12:56,845 --> 00:12:59,261
Ow! Shit!
Kathy.

171
00:12:59,295 --> 00:13:03,713
Why not let Maggie
make breakfast for once?
That's why we hired her.

172
00:13:03,748 --> 00:13:06,095
Dad, have you
tasted her cooking?

173
00:13:06,130 --> 00:13:09,719
Just that once.Hey, I heard that!

174
00:13:09,754 --> 00:13:11,066
MAGGIE:
I cook better than you.

175
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,481
ARTHUR:
We have to try to get along.

176
00:13:12,515 --> 00:13:13,689
[♪♪♪]

177
00:13:13,723 --> 00:13:15,380
KATHY:
Okay.

178
00:13:15,415 --> 00:13:19,350
Dad, will you tell Kathy
that keeping a record
of death is healthy.

179
00:13:19,384 --> 00:13:22,456
ARTHUR AND KATHY:
Keeping a record
of deaths is healthy.

180
00:13:22,491 --> 00:13:26,288
She's being a little slut about
it.Bobby.

181
00:13:26,322 --> 00:13:28,359
[COUGHS]Don't call your sister a slut.

182
00:13:28,393 --> 00:13:31,603
Thank you, Maggie.I prefer the term "bitch."

183
00:13:33,122 --> 00:13:35,124
See, sluts are girls
that have loose sex--

184
00:13:35,159 --> 00:13:38,369
Hey, Mr. Edgar Allen Poe,
did you do your homework?
Because Mr. Peterson told me--

185
00:13:38,403 --> 00:13:41,406
Aah! Damn it, Bobby!

186
00:13:41,441 --> 00:13:44,513
That's the third time
I've tripped on that stupid
scooter!

187
00:13:44,547 --> 00:13:46,204
Sorry.

188
00:13:46,239 --> 00:13:47,930
If we had a bigger place
we wouldn't have this problem--

189
00:13:47,965 --> 00:13:49,794
But we don't have
a big place anymore,
do we?

190
00:13:49,829 --> 00:13:52,590
This is the best
I can do for now.

191
00:13:52,624 --> 00:13:56,801
So let's try and keep our shit
off the floor.

192
00:13:56,836 --> 00:14:02,117
Now put away the damn tape
recorder. Will you do that for
me?
And get ready for school.

193
00:14:02,151 --> 00:14:05,292
BOBBY:
I'm sorry, Dad.

194
00:14:05,327 --> 00:14:07,363
[KNOCKING ON DOOR][ARTHUR SIGHS]

195
00:14:07,398 --> 00:14:10,539
Must be the lawyer. I forgot.What lawyer?

196
00:14:10,573 --> 00:14:14,405
Isn't our credit cleaned up?I don't think it's about that.

197
00:14:16,027 --> 00:14:18,927
Dad, they won't make
us move again, will they?

198
00:14:18,961 --> 00:14:23,241
It's gonna be all right.
Whatever it is, we'll deal with
it.

199
00:14:23,276 --> 00:14:26,175
Mr. Kriticos?That's right. You're...?

200
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:29,661
Ben Moss. How do you do?Please come in.

201
00:14:29,696 --> 00:14:34,114
Is now a good time, or...?Good a time as any.

202
00:14:34,149 --> 00:14:38,291
Please, just give me
one minute, will you?

203
00:14:40,569 --> 00:14:42,674
Okay. Sorry. I'm ready.

204
00:14:42,709 --> 00:14:46,678
I represent the estate of
your uncle Cyrus Kriticos.

205
00:14:46,713 --> 00:14:49,923
We have an Uncle Cyrus?Had.

206
00:14:49,958 --> 00:14:54,997
I only met him a couple of times
as a kid. He wasn't too popular.

207
00:14:55,032 --> 00:14:57,448
My dad said he
squandered the family fortune.

208
00:14:57,482 --> 00:15:01,693
We have a family fortune?Well, no. Cyrus squandered it.

209
00:15:01,728 --> 00:15:04,179
Hey, Bobby, isn't that great.
You got a late uncle.

210
00:15:04,213 --> 00:15:05,939
What is he late for?

211
00:15:05,974 --> 00:15:08,666
His next birthday.You mean he's dead?

212
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:11,393
KATHY: Now we his attention.ARTHUR: Pipe down.

213
00:15:11,427 --> 00:15:13,464
Cyrus recorded this
message six weeks ago.

214
00:15:13,498 --> 00:15:17,847
He asked that it be played
for you in the event of his
death.

215
00:15:17,882 --> 00:15:20,264
[♪♪♪]

216
00:15:25,441 --> 00:15:29,929
[ON SCREEN]
Arthur, it's good to talk to
you.

217
00:15:29,963 --> 00:15:34,002
 Sadly, if you're watching this,
it means I am dead.

218
00:15:34,036 --> 00:15:39,214
 Happily, that makes you
and your family my sole
beneficiaries.

219
00:15:39,248 --> 00:15:44,495
 I've instructed my lawyer, Mr.
Moss,
to deliver the essential
elements

220
00:15:44,529 --> 00:15:48,499
 in my last will and testament.
Give it to them, Ben.

221
00:15:54,643 --> 00:15:57,715
A key?A key to what?

222
00:15:57,749 --> 00:16:01,615
 A key to your new house. What?

223
00:16:01,650 --> 00:16:06,172
This house is the fruit
of my life's work.

224
00:16:06,206 --> 00:16:09,727
Bathrooms! Bathrooms!
Everyone gets their own
bathroom!

225
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:13,282
Is this for real? It is a one-of-a-kind home.

226
00:16:13,317 --> 00:16:16,044
 It's my home, actually.

227
00:16:17,528 --> 00:16:19,219
 My home.

228
00:16:19,254 --> 00:16:23,223
 I have no complaints.
I've led an interesting life.

229
00:16:23,258 --> 00:16:26,399
 I have seen some amazing
things.

230
00:16:28,677 --> 00:16:33,544
 My only regret is that I never
got to know my nephew, Arthur,

231
00:16:33,578 --> 00:16:36,064
 nor appreciate
the love of a family,

232
00:16:36,098 --> 00:16:37,789
 like you have. Dad.

233
00:16:37,824 --> 00:16:42,760
 This house is my attempt
to make up for that.

234
00:16:42,794 --> 00:16:44,486
 Enjoy.

235
00:16:47,282 --> 00:16:50,112
 Perhaps we'll meet again...

236
00:16:50,147 --> 00:16:53,115
 in another life.

237
00:16:56,153 --> 00:16:58,258
Wow!
When can we see it?

238
00:16:58,293 --> 00:17:00,260
The house is yours
whenever you like.

239
00:17:00,295 --> 00:17:01,951
Actually, I'm heading up
there after work.

240
00:17:01,986 --> 00:17:04,540
If you want, your wife andkids--Whoa!

241
00:17:04,575 --> 00:17:09,407
Time out. I am not the missushere.My wife...

242
00:17:09,442 --> 00:17:13,687
